{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChKqr9yqofq3ZtvE3FXA4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the plan for #161 to `.ard/161/plan.md` and the status file to `.ard/161/triage-engineer.md` (status done). I didn't run the build or any tests, since I only wrote the plan.\n\nThe plan sends `SIGUSR1` to a running `ard serve` to make every loop run one tick now. Each tick goes through the existing config reload and kill-switch check, so a paused controller still skips claims. A wake that arrives during a tick runs one more tick afterwards, and several wakes in a row count as one. I sized it M and rated the risk low.\n\nThe steps, in order:\n1. **Controller wake channel:** add a `Wake` channel to `Deps` in `internal/controller/controller.go`. A new goroutine logs `controller.wake` and signals each loop.\n2. **Scheduler:** in `internal/controller/scheduler.go`, the loop's wait also ends on a wake.\n3. **Signal handling:** new files `internal/servecmd/wake_unix.go` and `wake_other.go` turn `SIGUSR1` into wakes on Unix. Other platforms get no wake.\n4. **Wiring:** `internal/servecmd/serve.go` passes the wake channel into `controller.Deps`.\n5. **Docs:** update `docs/proposal.md` and `docs/runbooks/gate-2.md`. The runbook currently says to restart `serve`, so that advice gets replaced. `docs/TODO.md` is updated if it lists #161.\n\nThe test plan covers four scheduler cases and one signal test in `internal/servecmd/serve_test.go`. The scheduler cases are wake, wake while paused, coalescing, and wake during shutdown. The test command is `make test`, plus `make lint`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1892,"cache_read_input_tokens":32323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1892},"output_tokens":578,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"s